/-!
# The native canonical bundle in the holomorphic transition-data interface

The generic comparison is a genuine base-preserving, fibrewise
complex-linear biholomorphism between the canonical bundle obtained from
the tangent atlas and the bundle independently constructed from its
unit-valued reverse-Jacobian transitions.  Both directions use the
original total-space topologies and manifold atlases.

The specialization to the actual compact glued threefold preserves its
literal canonical fibres, all valid-chart coefficients, and their
intrinsic continuous alternating three-covectors.  It permits subsequent
bundle comparisons in the transition-data interface without replacing
the native canonical bundle by a formally named line bundle.
-/
